# invokeblock

- Label: Invoke Block
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2048
- Parameters: 7 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/invokeblock.html
- Summary (EN): Runs a block of COP nodes defined elsewhere on the layers wired into it, so a block can be reused in several places without copying or referencing individual nodes.
- Résumé (FR) : Exécute un bloc de nœuds COP défini ailleurs sur les couches branchées, avec itérations optionnelles, sans copier les nœuds.

- Inputs meaning: ["input#: ports set by the selected block's Block Begin inputs; populate them with Set Inputs and Outputs from Selected Block"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Block End Node", "meaning": "path to the Block End COP that ends the block to invoke"}, {"name": "Iterations", "meaning": "how many times to run the block, feeding outputs back as inputs"}, {"name": "Iterations Variable / Total Iterations Variable", "meaning": "context option names exposing the current and total iteration to expressions inside the block"}, {"name": "Inputs / Outputs", "meaning": "multiparameters defining the ports, matched by name to the block signature"}]

- Caveats: ["The node cannot cook cable outputs.", "Repeated iterations occur only when outputs match inputs by index; otherwise it runs once and shows a warning.", "Compiled COP networks do not support simulation."]

